{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" query fails (the query function throws an error), React Query will automatically retry the query if that query's request has not reached the max number of consecutive retries (defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3"},{"type":"text","value":") or a function is provided to determine if a retry is allowed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can configure retries both on a global level and an individual query level."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retry = false"},{"type":"text","value":" will disable retries."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retry = 6"},{"type":"text","value":" will retry failing requests 6 times before showing the final error thrown by the function."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retry = true"},{"type":"text","value":" will infinitely retry failing requests."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retry = (failureCount, error) => ..."},{"type":"text","value":" allows for custom logic based on why the request failed."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useQuery } from 'react-query'\n\n// Make a specific query retry a certain number of times\nconst result = useQuery(['todos', 1], fetchTodoListPage, {\n  retry: 10, // Will retry failed requests 10 times before displaying an error\n})","lang":"js"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"retry-delay","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retry Delay"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, retries in React Query do not happen immediately after a request fails. As is standard, a back-off delay is gradually applied to each retry attempt."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retryDelay"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to double (starting at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1000"},{"type":"text","value":"ms) with each attempt, but not exceed 30 seconds:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Configure for all queries\nimport { QueryCache, QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from 'react-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      retryDelay: attemptIndex => Math.min(1000 * 2 ** attemptIndex, 30000),\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>...</QueryClientProvider>\n}","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Though it is not recommended, you can obviously override the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retryDelay"},{"type":"text","value":" function/integer in both the Provider and individual query options. If set to an integer instead of a function the delay will always be the same amount of time:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const result = useQuery('todos', fetchTodoList, {\n  retryDelay: 1000, // Will always wait 1000ms to retry, regardless of how many retries\n})","lang":"js"}],"headings":[{"id":"retry-delay","text":"Retry Delay","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWhen a `useQuery` query fails (the query function throws an error), React Query will automatically retry the query if that query's request has not reached the max number of consecutive retries (defaults to `3`) or a function is provided to determine if a retry is allowed.\n\nYou can configure retries both on a global level and an individual query level.\n\n- Setting `retry = false` will disable retries.\n- Setting `retry = 6` will retry failing requests 6 times before showing the final error thrown by the function.\n- Setting `retry = true` will infinitely retry failing requests.\n- Setting `retry = (failureCount, error) => ...` allows for custom logic based on why the request failed.\n\n```js\nimport { useQuery } from 'react-query'\n\n// Make a specific query retry a certain number of times\nconst result = useQuery(['todos', 1], fetchTodoListPage, {\n  retry: 10, // Will retry failed requests 10 times before displaying an error\n})\n```\n\n## Retry Delay\n\nBy default, retries in React Query do not happen immediately after a request fails. As is standard, a back-off delay is gradually applied to each retry attempt.\n\nThe default `retryDelay` is set to double (starting at `1000`ms) with each attempt, but not exceed 30 seconds:\n\n```js\n// Configure for all queries\nimport { QueryCache, QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from 'react-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      retryDelay: attemptIndex => Math.min(1000 * 2 ** attemptIndex, 30000),\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>...</QueryClientProvider>\n}\n```\n\nThough it is not recommended, you can obviously override the `retryDelay` function/integer in both the Provider and individual query options. If set to an integer instead of a function the delay will always be the same amount of time:\n\n```js\nconst result = useQuery('todos', fetchTodoList, {\n  retryDelay: 1000, // Will always wait 1000ms to retry, regardless of how many retries\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: query-retries\ntitle: Query Retries\n---\n\nWhen a `useQuery` query fails (the query function throws an error), React Query will automatically retry the query if that query's request has not reached the max number of consecutive retries (defaults to `3`) or a function is provided to determine if a retry is allowed.\n\nYou can configure retries both on a global level and an individual query level.\n\n- Setting `retry = false` will disable retries.\n- Setting `retry = 6` will retry failing requests 6 times before showing the final error thrown by the function.\n- Setting `retry = true` will infinitely retry failing requests.\n- Setting `retry = (failureCount, error) => ...` allows for custom logic based on why the request failed.\n\n```js\nimport { useQuery } from 'react-query'\n\n// Make a specific query retry a certain number of times\nconst result = useQuery(['todos', 1], fetchTodoListPage, {\n  retry: 10, // Will retry failed requests 10 times before displaying an error\n})\n```\n\n## Retry Delay\n\nBy default, retries in React Query do not happen immediately after a request fails. As is standard, a back-off delay is gradually applied to each retry attempt.\n\nThe default `retryDelay` is set to double (starting at `1000`ms) with each attempt, but not exceed 30 seconds:\n\n```js\n// Configure for all queries\nimport { QueryCache, QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from 'react-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      retryDelay: attemptIndex => Math.min(1000 * 2 ** attemptIndex, 30000),\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>...</QueryClientProvider>\n}\n```\n\nThough it is not recommended, you can obviously override the `retryDelay` function/integer in both the Provider and individual query options. If set to an integer instead of a function the delay will always be the same amount of time:\n\n```js\nconst result = useQuery('todos', fetchTodoList, {\n  retryDelay: 1000, // Will always wait 1000ms to retry, regardless of how many retries\n})\n```\n"}
